course: dictionary
lesson: 2464
title: Darken: getting darker, and feeling darker too
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Darken is a verb, so it describes something that happens or something you do. Its simplest meaning is to become darker, or to make something darker. «In industrial England, soot darkened trees» means the soot made the trees darker. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Darker fits, so you are on the right track.
explain: Darken can also describe a mood or a face. «The weather often warns you: tall dark clouds, a darkening sky, a sudden cool wind and distant rumbles» shows the sky getting darker before a storm. A face can darken too, when someone becomes angry or upset. The context tells you which meaning is being used.
explain: Watch out for the idiom «Never darken my door again.» Here darken does not mean becoming dark at all. When a phrase does not make literal sense, it is probably an idiom, so do not try to picture it. Read the whole sentence and think about what the speaker means.
fact: Darken is a verb: darken, darkens, darkened, darkening.
fact: «Darken» means to become darker, or to make something darker.
fact: «Darken» can also mean to become sad, angry or less hopeful, as a face or mood can.
fact: In science lessons on light, a room darkens when you close the curtains.
fact: «Never darken my door again» means never come to my house again.
exercise: «The sky darkened before the storm.» What does darkened mean here? | *Became darker | Became louder | Became warmer | Became lighter
exercise: «Her face darkened with anger.» What does darkened suggest? | Became lighter in colour | Became clean and shiny | Became smaller and shrank | *Became angry or upset
exercise: «The Rat marches into the darkening wood.» Find and copy the word that tells you the wood is getting darker. | into | marches | the | *darkening
test: «The blast darkened the sky for months or years.» How long did the sky stay dark? | Never at all | For exactly one second | *For months or years | Only for one afternoon
test: Dad says, «Never darken my door again.» What does he mean? | The front door is broken and will not open | Turn off all the lights in the house | Paint the front door black | *Never come to my house again
exam: «Weather often warns you before it turns dangerous: tall dark clouds, a darkening sky, a sudden cool wind and distant rumbles.» Which word shows the sky is getting darker? | Tall | *Darkening | Rumbles | Warns
